# build/hosts.env.example - T137a. Variable NAMES and their meaning only. The real file is build/hosts.env: gitignored, mode 0600,
# never committed, no secret in it (a key FILE is named here, never the key). scripts/build/dispatch.sh reads its host list ONLY from
# that file and refuses a submit when it is absent or names no host (REFUSED reason=no_qualified_host).
# The bootstrap build host is the one recorded by T100 and confirmed by the owner at HC-1b (T102); until then no host qualifies and
# every dispatched build ends blocked-unavailable (T006a, BLOCKED-ON ODG-07). Hosts are tried in the order of their number, at submit time only.
#
# BUILD_HOST_<n>        SSH destination of the n-th build host, user@address (n = 1, 2, ...: the order of preference)
# BUILD_HOST_<n>_ROLE   free text, the role the owner confirmed at HC-1b (for example: primary-build)
# BUILD_HOST_<n>_CAPACITY  free text, the capacity class the owner confirmed at HC-1b
# BUILD_HOST_<n>_FP     pinned SSH host-key fingerprint, taken from docs/infrastructure/build-hosts.md (T100); the dispatcher never trusts on first use
# BUILD_SSH_IDENTITY    absolute path of the hub's SSH private key FILE, outside the checkout, mode 0600 (never an agent socket: a supervisor restart would lose it)
BUILD_HOST_1=
BUILD_HOST_1_ROLE=
BUILD_HOST_1_CAPACITY=
BUILD_HOST_1_FP=
BUILD_SSH_IDENTITY=
